---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const BRAND_NAME = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_BRAND_NAME ?? 'Aura: Looksmaxxing';
const SITE_URL = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL ?? 'https://www.aura-looksmaxxing.com';

const breadcrumbSchema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": `${SITE_URL}/` },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "About", "item": `${SITE_URL}/about` },
  ],
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`About | ${BRAND_NAME}`}
  description={`${BRAND_NAME} is an AI-powered looksmaxxing platform built to help you unlock your best look.`}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)} />
  </Fragment>
  <section class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-24">

    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-black text-white mb-10">About {BRAND_NAME}</h1>

    <div class="space-y-6 text-[#888] leading-relaxed">

      <p>
        {BRAND_NAME} is an AI-powered platform built for anyone serious about improving their appearance.
        We combine face analysis, hairstyle try-on, personalized glow-up routines, and an AI coaching assistant
        into one simple tool.
      </p>

      <p>
        The idea is straightforward: looksmaxxing advice should be data-driven, personalized, and accessible.
        No guesswork, just an honest PSL score, a potential score, and a concrete plan to get there.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white pt-6">How the analysis works</h2>

      <p>
        You upload a frontal photo, taken with a neutral expression under even lighting. A side profile at
        roughly 90 degrees is optional, but it measurably improves bone structure analysis, particularly the
        gonial angle and jawline modeling. Rear camera, around two metres of distance, and no wide-angle lens:
        wide lenses distort facial proportions and will skew the result.
      </p>

      <p>
        From those photos the model reads more than ten facial metrics, among them gonial angle, midface
        ratio, cheekbone prominence, canthal tilt, interpupillary distance, skin clarity, hairline depth and
        an asymmetry index. Those measurements are scored against established looksmaxxing frameworks to
        produce a PSL rating on the familiar 1 to 10 scale, along with a separate potential score that
        estimates where the same face could realistically land.
      </p>

      <p>
        The gap between those two numbers is what the glow-up plan works on. Because the recommendations are
        derived from your own measurements rather than a generic template, two people with the same PSL score
        will usually get different plans.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white pt-6">What Aura is not</h2>

      <p>
        Attractiveness ratings are not an exact science, and we would rather say so plainly. The analysis
        gives you a consistent, repeatable baseline and a sense of which features move the needle for your
        face. It is not a medical assessment, not a surgical consultation, and not a substitute for a
        qualified professional. Anything involving a procedure deserves a real practitioner.
      </p>

      <p>
        We also do not promise a number. The potential score is a modelled estimate, not a guarantee, and
        structural change in adults is slow when it happens at all. The parts of looksmaxxing that reliably
        work for most people, such as skin, hair, grooming, body composition and posture, are exactly the
        parts the plan spends most of its attention on.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white pt-6">Your photos</h2>

      <p>
        Photos are processed securely and are never shared with third parties. They are retained only as long
        as delivering your analysis requires, and you can request deletion of your data at any time by
        contacting support. The full detail is in our <a href="/privacy" class="text-fuchsia-400 hover:text-fuchsia-300">privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white pt-6">Learn before you subscribe</h2>

      <p>
        Most of what we know is public. The <a href="/blog" class="text-fuchsia-400 hover:text-fuchsia-300">guides</a>
        cover the underlying anatomy and the techniques in depth, the
        <a href="/glossary" class="text-fuchsia-400 hover:text-fuchsia-300">glossary</a> explains the community
        terminology, and the <a href="/tools" class="text-fuchsia-400 hover:text-fuchsia-300">free tools</a> let you
        try the basics without an account. Pricing is on the
        <a href="/pricing" class="text-fuchsia-400 hover:text-fuchsia-300">pricing page</a>, and common questions are
        answered in the <a href="/faq" class="text-fuchsia-400 hover:text-fuchsia-300">FAQ</a>.
      </p>

      <p>
        Questions or feedback? Reach out anytime.
      </p>

    </div>

    <div class="mt-12">
      <a
        href={`mailto:support@${new URL(SITE_URL).hostname}`}
        class="flex items-center gap-2 bg-[#111] border border-[#222] rounded-xl px-5 py-3 text-white text-sm hover:border-[#444] transition-colors w-fit"
      >
        Contact Us
      </a>
    </div>

  </section>
</BaseLayout>
